ef=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T14:54:12-07:00","id":1418720,"title":"","content":"I was asking if the writers of Ordo Dracul named that bloodline after the Moroi from Vampire Academy. Thanks \ud83d\ude0a. You answered my question.<br /> <br /> Sorry. I wasn\u2019t sure about the dates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T18:14:04-07:00","id":1418747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367397-twice-cursed-variants?p=1418720#post1418720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was asking if the writers of Ordo Dracul named that bloodline after the Moroi from Vampire Academy. Thanks \ud83d\ude0a. You answered my question.<br /> <br /> Sorry. I wasn\u2019t sure about the dates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to help!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T06:17:37-07:00","id":1418998,"title":"","content":"I like it, a lot. See no problem with the Discipline spread overlap if you do Mekhet/Nosferatu and Daeva/Mekhet. Especially because to an outsider, they might all seem like one type. Then, upon investigation, it's found out they are different... And this freaks the Kindred out. Are they proto-Clans, or are the Clans becoming something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T04:39:20-08:00","id":1424905,"title":"","content":"My apologies Yossarian, couldn't wait. Though need some help finishing them up. Something occurred to me regarding the ones with Celerity, Obfuscate, Vigor: they're made up of three of the (arguably) oldest Clans. Could tie in with the whole what vampire\u2019s were before they became Clans.<br /> <br /> Daeva/Mekhet: The xxx<br /> Xxx gain Dream Visions and Kiss of the Succubus for free at character creation.<br /> Xxx can only Embrace humans with\u2026<br /> Clan Bane (the Wayward Curse): xxx gain both the Daeva and Mekhet and banes at Humanity 6.<br /> <br /> Favored Attributes: Manipulation and Wits<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Celerity, Obfuscate, Vigor<br /> <br /> Mekhet/Nosferatu: The Ominous<br /> Ominous gain Dream Visions and Unsettling Gaze for free at character creation.<br /> Ominous can only Embrace humans that have died.<br /> Clan Bane (the Inhuman Curse): Ominous gain both the Mekhet and Nosferatu banes at Humanity 6.<br /> <br /> Favored Attributes: Intelligence and Strength<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Celerity, Obfuscate, Vigor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T16:51:07-08:00","id":1425266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PJ123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367397-twice-cursed-variants?p=1424905#post1424905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My apologies Yossarian, couldn't wait. Though need some help finishing them up. Something occurred to me regarding the ones with Celerity, Obfuscate, Vigor: they're made up of three of the (arguably) oldest Clans. Could tie in with the whole what vampire\u2019s were before they became Clans.<br /> <br /> Daeva/Mekhet: The xxx<br /> Xxx gain Dream Visions and Kiss of the Succubus for free at character creation.<br /> Xxx can only Embrace humans with\u2026<br /> Clan Bane (the Wayward Curse): xxx gain both the Daeva and Mekhet and banes at Humanity 6.<br /> <br /> Favored Attributes: Manipulation and Wits<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Celerity, Obfuscate, Vigor<br /> <br /> Mekhet/Nosferatu: The Ominous<br /> Ominous gain Dream Visions and Unsettling Gaze for free at character creation.<br /> Ominous can only Embrace humans that have died.<br /> Clan Bane (the Inhuman Curse): Ominous gain both the Mekhet and Nosferatu banes at Humanity 6.<br /> <br /> Favored Attributes: Intelligence and Strength<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Celerity, Obfuscate, Vigor</div> </div> </div> </div>These are both really cool. For the Daevkhet, the archetype is maybe like a love story involving ghosts. The suave, dead Don Juan, who comes to you in your dreams but also can't cross salt lines. Not sure how to crystallize that into a single word. Maybe they can only Embrace people who are a ghost's anchor?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T18:20:01-08:00","id":1425289,"title":"","content":"Thanks, but you (and thesaurus \ud83d\ude01) did most work. I just had to figure out which two favored attributes (interestingly enough, by adding in these two Twice-Cursed, each of the favored attributes gets used twice).<br /> <br /> What about the Obsessed? Only being able to embrace Anchors sounds cool. Their Dream Visions lead them to a mortal, their Daeva curse takes over, so they drain and Embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-21T00:38:04-08:00","id":1425327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PJ123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367397-twice-cursed-variants?p=1425289#post1425289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, but you (and thesaurus \ud83d\ude01) did most work. I just had to figure out which two favored attributes (interestingly enough, by adding in these two Twice-Cursed, each of the favored attributes gets used twice).<br /> <br /> What about the Obsessed? Only being able to embrace Anchors sounds cool. Their Dream Visions lead them to a mortal, their Daeva curse takes over, so they drain and Embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obsessed is excellent! And yeah, that &quot;man of your dreams turns out to be dead&quot; trope is definitely how I'd do them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","